task.claim:
For each curve whose 4q - t^2 is completely factored (P-192, P-224, P-256,
P-384, P-521, B-163, B-233, B-283, B-409, B-571, Curve25519 = Ed25519,
and Curve448 = Ed448, Ed448-Goldilocks), with q, t, D_K, f and the
factorisation as recorded in nist.json:
  t^2 - 4q = D_K * f^2;
  4q - t^2 = prod p_i^e_i (the factorisation certificate);
  D_K = -core or -4*core, with core the product of the odd-exponent p_i,
    as nist.exact_discriminant computes it, and D_K is a discriminant;
  min_nonscalar_degree(D_K) is the value nist.json reports;
  and, if the listed factors are prime, D_K is a fundamental discriminant.
